  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 140 PM CDT Thu Sep 10 2026\n\nOn Sunday, upper-level high pressure finds itself in the \nsoutheastern US, as a synoptic-scale upper-level trough extending \nfrom Canada to the four-corners region makes its way east from the \nPacific. While Sunday will likely remain hot and dry, this pattern \nshift will place the Panhandles in SW upper-level flow, allowing for \na more sustained and larger scale weather pattern to set up through \nthe beginning of next week. Sustained SW flow over the Rockies will \nallow for repeated lee-side troughing and upper-level support \nthroughout next week. While the exact scope of this weather event is \nuncertain, widespread daily PoP chances Monday-Wednesday are on the \ntable. As we near the end of the forecast period, the end of next \nweek hints at the possibility of an upper-level low forming over the \nsouthern plains landing the Panhandles in NW upper-level flow, which \ncould allow for PoP chances to extend into the later half of the \nweek as well.",
